From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] Define native COM mass and source-time contracts

DRAFT PATCH AGAINST 4be6ab0d50a63eee512e4d16d075b9fee90e552f

This patch is intentionally stored rather than applied automatically. Apply it
in a configured ASPECT worktree, build, run the focused tests, regenerate test
baselines, and only then remove the temporary disable guard.

Key changes:

* require an explicit positive total reference mass for the native COM frame;
* use the same committed/current source time layer for internal potential,
  dipole, inertia, and displaced density sheets;
* include the normalized COM constraint residual in convergence;
* stop requiring angular-momentum projection for fixed-inner models;
* continue rejecting post-solve translational projections.

